WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.850
- [Narrator] Russian
President Vladimir Putin said

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.340
that Moscow would
suspend its participation

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.640
in the last remaining major
nuclear arms control treaty

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.552
between the US and Russia,
the New START treaty.

00:00:12.552 --> 00:00:16.943
(Vladimir speaking in Russian)

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:17.984
- [Reporter] Mr. President, any reaction

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.673
to Putin saying he's
pulling out of New START?

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:22.770
- Big mistake.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.200
- [Narrator] Here's what
the New START treaty is

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.240
and what Russia's suspension means

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.313
for global nuclear arms control.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.470
The New START, meaning New
Strategic Arms Reduction Treaty

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.110
was signed in Prague in 2010

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.390
by former President Barack Obama

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.020
and former Russian
President, Dmitry Medvedev.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.640
It was an extension to START
I, which was signed in 1991.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.160
This was a way to try to reset relations

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.490
between Russia and the
US after the Cold War.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.990
The agreement was important

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.443
because these two countries
hold approximately 90%

00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:02.400
of the world's nuclear weapons,
so the pact was created

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.463
to make sure this arsenal was controlled.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.950
The treaty limits the number

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:11.130
of strategic nuclear
warheads that can be deployed

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.380
by either Russia or the US

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.670
to 1,550 and allows both sides

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.793
to inspect each other's
nuclear facilities.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:25.290
Vladimir Putin said it was
time to suspend this deal

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:29.220
because Russia feels the US
has not abided by the agreement

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.380
by not allowing Russian inspectors

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.630
on US nuclear sites.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.670
The US said it is Russia

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:39.030
that is blocking onsite inspections.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.330
NATO Secretary General
urged Vladimir Putin

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.430
to reconsider the suspension.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.230
- We have to remember that this is one

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.890
of the last major arms
control agreements we have.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.810
- [Narrator] The Foreign
Ministry has said,

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.030
following Mr. Putin's announcement

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.770
that Russia would continue

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.780
to observe the limits on the number

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.320
of nuclear warheads it can
deploy under the treaty.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.310
And he also said

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.610
that Russia would continue to
notify the US when it plans

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.970
to test launch intercontinental
ballistic missiles

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:12.096
and submarine launch ballistic missiles.

00:02:12.096 --> 00:02:16.013
(Vladimir speaking in Russian)

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.930
- We'll be watching carefully

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.820
to see what Russia actually does.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.100
We'll, of course, make
sure that in any of that,

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.100
we are postured appropriately
for the security

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.980
of our own country,
and that of our allies.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.450
- [Narrator] This suspension means

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.060
that the US will lose
access to inspect some

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.130
of Russia's nuclear facilities.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.710
And it's worrisome because
what Russia is planning,

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:41.640
whatever that is, it could
become more shrouded in secrecy.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.100
But moreover, it calls into question

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.720
whether or not this agreement

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:49.442
to control nuclear weapons
can actually last now.

00:02:49.442 --> 00:02:51.270
(nationalistic music)

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.190
China, for example, has indicated

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.980
that it wants to build
a large nuclear arsenal.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.200
North Korea, as we know, has been testing

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.770
intercontinental ballistic
missiles and there's also concern

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:05.310
among Western officials that
Iran might actually be close

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.985
to making bomb grade nuclear fuel.

00:03:07.985 --> 00:03:09.720
(nationalistic music)

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.400
The Journal spoke to the director

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.940
of the Pro-Kremlin Institute
for Political Studies who said

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.790
that if Washington doesn't
listen to Moscow now,

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.700
Putin may officially
withdraw from the treaty.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.550
And if that happens, we
could expect a change

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.969
that would reduce the
US's nuclear security.

00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:29.719
(dramatic music)

